From f924c9a8b21520afa4046129dfb9f31c8d0da0de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:56:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] devfs: mconfig's cb and mp are volatile (set after waserror,
 used by its handler)

A local that changed after its waserror() is indeterminate in the
handler unless it is volatile (C11 7.13.2.1, as 0066 and the namec
patch); a compiler that keeps it in a register hands back its value at
waserror time.  In mconfig:

- cb: set to nil, then waserror(), then parseconfig(a, n, &cb, &ct),
  which sets *cbp first and then raises its usage errors (and
  lookupcmd's); "bad hexkey" follows.  The handler's free(cb) freed the
  nil and the Cmdbuf leaked.  parseconfig takes a Cmdbuf *volatile*.
- mp: nil, then the write lock's waserror(), then devalloc; an error
  after it (Enomem for an Inner, setdsize's "starts after device end")
  goes to Fail, whose mdeldev(mp) saw nil: the half-made device stayed
  in its tree.

Found by reading (a scan for locals changed after waserror(),
2026-11-27); compiled with gcc and clang, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/src/9/port/devfs.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/src/9/port/devfs.c b/sys/src/9/port/devfs.c
index 0126869b9..508698827 100644
--- a/sys/src/9/port/devfs.c
+++ b/sys/src/9/port/devfs.c
@@ -498,7 +498,7 @@ validdevname(Tree *t, char *dname)
 }
 
 static void
-parseconfig(char *a, long n, Cmdbuf **cbp, Cmdtab **ctp)
+parseconfig(char *a, long n, Cmdbuf *volatile *cbp, Cmdtab **ctp)
 {
 	Cmdbuf	*cb;
 	Cmdtab	*ct;
@@ -571,9 +571,9 @@ mconfig(char* a, long n)
 	uchar	key[2*256/8];
 	int	keylen;
 	Chan	**idev;
-	Cmdbuf	*cb;
+	Cmdbuf	*volatile cb;	/* parseconfig sets it after waserror, the handler frees it */
 	Cmdtab	*ct;
-	Fsdev	*mp;
+	Fsdev	*volatile mp;	/* devalloc sets it after waserror, Fail deletes it */
 	Inner	*inprv;
 	Tree	*t;
 
-- 
